# Project notes for Claude

<!-- A starter CLAUDE.md. Copy this to claude/default.md (for every new project) or
     claude/<machine>.md (for one), and make it yours. Gleipnir copies it into a new
     project once, when the machine is first set up, and only if the project doesn't
     already have a CLAUDE.md. After that it's the project's file: edit it there,
     and commit it if you want to keep it. -->

## About this project

- What it is, and who it's for.
- The main parts and where they live, e.g. `src/routes` for pages, `src/lib/server` for server-only code.

## Stack

- Framework, language and versions, e.g. SvelteKit with TypeScript.
- Database and how it's accessed, e.g. PostgreSQL through an ORM.
- Styling, e.g. Tailwind CSS.

## Commands

- Install: `npm ci`
- Type and lint checks: `npm run check`, `npm run lint`
- Tests: `npm test`, and `npx playwright test` for end-to-end tests
- Don't start the dev server; it's already running.

## How I work

- Before a larger change, outline your plan in a few lines and wait for me to agree.
- Keep changes small and focused on the request. Mention anything else you notice instead of changing it.
- Ask when something is unclear rather than guessing.
- After each change, run the checks and tests above and fix anything you broke.

## Code style

- Follow the patterns already in the codebase before inventing new ones.
- Prefer clear names and small functions over comments.
- No new dependencies without asking first.

## Don't

- Don't edit generated files or anything in `node_modules`.
- Don't change config files (build, lint, CI) unless I ask.